title: Change the Central Executive Committee
subtitle: The final composition of its three seats, in one decision.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
card-image: img/polish/polish_party_advisers.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_party_rules && PolishParty.advisersAvailable(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card party.advisers (technical reference 10.4.2; card catalogue 6.5; Z — 0.35: a separate card): 1 T,
// cd 6 M; it does not reset the adviser cooldown. Próchnik, Drobner and Dubois belong to the continuation.
Q.pl_adv_draft = PolishParty.activeAdvisers(Q).join(',');
PolishParty.advisersView(Q);
!}

= Change the Central Executive Committee

The present Committee: [+ pl_adv_draft_text +]. A first appointment strengthens the person's faction (+5 strength, −5 dissent); a dismissal adds +5 dissent; a return gives nothing new.

- @compose
- @easy_discard

@compose
title: Compose the Committee
go-to: menu

@menu
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersView(Q);
!}

= The new Committee

Chosen: [+ pl_adv_draft_text +]. Nothing is spent until you confirm.

- @toggle_daszynski
- @toggle_puzak
- @toggle_perl
- @toggle_niedzialkowski
- @toggle_arciszewski
- @toggle_zaremba
- @toggle_czapinski
- @toggle_jaworowski
- @toggle_moraczewski
- @toggle_ziemiecki
- @toggle_malinowski
- @confirm
- @polish_party_advisers: Start again.

@toggle_daszynski
title: Ignacy Daszyński
subtitle: **Centrum.** Austrian Reichsrat deputy 1897–1918; in November 1918 he headed the Provisional People’s Government in Lublin. Since 1919 a deputy to the Sejm Ustawodawczy and member of the PPS CKW; deputy prime minister 1920–1921. [+ pl_adv_daszynski_actions +] [+ pl_adv_daszynski_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_daszynski_in = 1 or pl_adv_daszynski_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'daszynski');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_puzak
title: Kazimierz Pużak
subtitle: **Centrum.** A political prisoner of tsarist Russia 1911–1917, from 1915 in the Schlüsselburg fortress. Since 1919 a PPS deputy to the Sejm Ustawodawczy and member of the party’s Rada Naczelna; in 1920 deputy head of the CKW Military Department. [+ pl_adv_puzak_actions +] [+ pl_adv_puzak_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_puzak_in = 1 or pl_adv_puzak_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'puzak');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_perl
title: Feliks Perl
subtitle: **Centrum.** Co-founder and leading ideologue of the PPS (Paris congress, 1892) and editor-in-chief of the party daily Robotnik; since 1919 a PPS deputy to the Sejm Ustawodawczy. [+ pl_adv_perl_actions +] [+ pl_adv_perl_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_perl_in = 1 or pl_adv_perl_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'perl');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_niedzialkowski
title: Mieczysław Niedziałkowski
subtitle: **Centrum.** A PPS theorist. In 1918 head of the Sejm department of the Interior Ministry; since 1919 a deputy to the Sejm Ustawodawczy, secretary of its Constitutional Committee and member of the PPS CKW. [+ pl_adv_niedzialkowski_actions +] [+ pl_adv_niedzialkowski_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_niedzialkowski_in = 1 or pl_adv_niedzialkowski_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'niedzialkowski');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_arciszewski
title: Tomasz Arciszewski
subtitle: **Centrum.** In PPS since 1896 and one of the leaders of its Combat Organisation; in November 1918 minister of labour in the Lublin government, then minister of posts and telegraphs until January 1919; since 1919 a deputy to the Sejm Ustawodawczy. [+ pl_adv_arciszewski_actions +] [+ pl_adv_arciszewski_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_arciszewski_in = 1 or pl_adv_arciszewski_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'arciszewski');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_zaremba
title: Zygmunt Zaremba
subtitle: **Lewica.** A socialist since 1912; in 1917 he led the Polish socialists of southern Russia. In 1918–1919 he represented PPS on the executive of the Warsaw Council of Workers’ Delegates; a member of the PPS CKW and Rada Naczelna. [+ pl_adv_zaremba_actions +] [+ pl_adv_zaremba_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_zaremba_in = 1 or pl_adv_zaremba_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'zaremba');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_czapinski
title: Kazimierz Czapiński
subtitle: **Lewica.** A socialist publicist born in Minsk, in the Galician PPSD from 1910; since 1919 a deputy to the Sejm Ustawodawczy and secretary of the socialist deputies’ club; since 1921 a member of the PPS CKW. [+ pl_adv_czapinski_actions +] [+ pl_adv_czapinski_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_czapinski_in = 1 or pl_adv_czapinski_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'czapinski');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_jaworowski
title: Rajmund Jaworowski
subtitle: **Piłsudczycy.** A PPS militant and in 1914–1915 an intelligence officer of the Legions; since 1918 chairman of the PPS Warsaw District Workers’ Committee, a Warsaw city councillor and, since 1921, a member of the PPS CKW. [+ pl_adv_jaworowski_actions +] [+ pl_adv_jaworowski_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_jaworowski_in = 1 or pl_adv_jaworowski_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'jaworowski');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_moraczewski
title: Jędrzej Moraczewski
subtitle: **Piłsudczycy.** Prime minister of Poland’s first central government (November 1918 – January 1919). Since 1919 vice-marshal of the Sejm Ustawodawczy and member of the PPS CKW; from 1920 a vice-chairman of the railway workers’ union. [+ pl_adv_moraczewski_actions +] [+ pl_adv_moraczewski_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_moraczewski_in = 1 or pl_adv_moraczewski_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'moraczewski');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_ziemiecki
title: Bronisław Ziemięcki
subtitle: **Piłsudczycy.** Minister of industry in the Lublin government in November 1918, then minister of labour and social welfare under Moraczewski until January 1919; since 1919 a deputy to the Sejm Ustawodawczy. [+ pl_adv_ziemiecki_actions +] [+ pl_adv_ziemiecki_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_ziemiecki_in = 1 or pl_adv_ziemiecki_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'ziemiecki');
!}
go-to: menu

@toggle_malinowski
title: Marian Malinowski
subtitle: **Piłsudczycy.** A PPS militant from the Radom district who twice escaped tsarist exile. In November 1918 minister of public works in the Lublin government, then minister without portfolio under Moraczewski; since 1919 a deputy to the Sejm Ustawodawczy. [+ pl_adv_malinowski_actions +] [+ pl_adv_malinowski_state +]
choose-if: pl_adv_malinowski_in = 1 or pl_adv_malinowski_can_add = 1
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersToggle(Q, 'malinowski');
!}
go-to: menu

@confirm
title: Confirm the Committee
subtitle: [+ pl_adv_confirm_note +]
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.advisersStatus(Q, String(Q.pl_adv_draft || '').split(',').filter(Boolean)).available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_adv_confirm_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.advisersChoose(Q, String(Q.pl_adv_draft || '').split(',').filter(Boolean));
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true

= Change the Central Executive Committee

